 [17592186364480 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535745 true] [17592186364480 1100 "A linear system of ODEs has the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}=[1,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Two linearly independent eigenvectors of the system's matrix are ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}.$ After shifting using $u=x-{x}^{∗},$ the system becomes ${u}^{′}=Au.$ Which of the following is **guaranteed** to be an eigenvector of the matrix $A?$" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364480 1113 #uuid "331c7839-3f32-5d34-bd91-dc6188dfcb86" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364480 1145 "After shifting a linear system, the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors remain unchanged.\n\nThus, the matrix $A$ in the shifted system has the same eigenvectors as the system's matrix in the original coordinates. These eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ or any nonzero vectors that are parallel to them.\n\nAmong the given options, the only vector that is nonzero and is guaranteed to be parallel to either ${v}_{1}$ or ${v}_{2}$ is the vector $-{v}_{2}.$" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364482 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364483 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364484 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364485 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364486 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1041 "selection" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364483 13194139535745 true] [17592186364481 1110 #uuid "2f4e7885-dea3-5caa-be8f-f91f213b7a94" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364482 1034 "{v}_{2}-{x}^{∗}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364482 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364482 1111 #uuid "4296219e-6e3d-5b72-9d74-55c5e1801055" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364483 1034 "-{v}_{2}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364483 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364483 1111 #uuid "e1e15ba5-d7f4-545e-990a-40d4cf85497f" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364484 1034 "{v}_{1}+{x}^{∗}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364484 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364484 1111 #uuid "a4c21628-6c25-50a4-aa86-2323e98849a1" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364485 1034 "0" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364485 1111 #uuid "8f8459dc-570f-5a69-917c-239023a47cdc" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364486 1034 "{x}^{∗}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364486 1111 #uuid "5606a964-87de-5574-b471-d69242c7e2ae" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364487 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364488 13194139535745 true] [17592186364487 1089 "q-335073" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364487 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535745 true] [17592186364487 1100 "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364487 1113 #uuid "f439789e-cdab-5342-8d21-9a3ce1e3d364" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364487 1145 "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{al