d equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =4x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+y(t)-12 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =4(u(t)+3)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)-12 \\\\  & =4u(t)+12-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)-12 \\\\  & =4u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=4u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364545 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364546 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364547 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364548 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364549 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1041 "selection" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364549 13194139535745 true] [17592186364544 1110 #uuid "928af578-3572-5ce4-9e81-766db94481bd" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364545 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)+2v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=4u(t)-2{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364545 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364545 1111 #uuid "af503d8b-c15e-5e59-ac0d-212d448386ce" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364546 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=4u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364546 1111 #uuid "94da8e6a-7eda-5ff7-a693-d44f4d150fc2" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364547 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=u(t)+2{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=4{u}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364547 1111 #uuid "c00de80c-b463-5e54-8f75-48bf7cb52405" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364548 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+2{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364548 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364548 1111 #uuid "9910db5c-b93e-58bb-bb04-1af03685b359" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364549 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=4u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364549 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535745 true] [17592186364549 1111 #uuid "b4b679d3-ab73-5fc6-9c11-d05704140bc9" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364550 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364551 13194139535745 true] [17592186364550 1089 "q-335485" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364550 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535745 true] [17592186364550 1100 "A linear system of ODEs has the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}=[-2,\\,4]^{T}.$ The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}.$ After shifting using $u=x-{x}^{∗},$ the system becomes ${u}^{′}=Au.$ Which of the following is **guaranteed** to be an eigenvalue of the matrix $A?$" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364550 1113 #uuid "dbd0072c-9617-5dfd-8c07-1e1b8ec76bf7" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364550 1145 "After shifting a linear system, the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors remain unchanged.\n\nThus, the matrix $A$ in the shifted system has the same eigenvalues as the system's matrix in the original coordinates. These eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ or any expressions that are equal to them.\n\nAmong the given options, the only quantity that is guaranteed to be an eigenvalue of $A$ is ${\\lambda }_{2}.$" 13194139535745 true] [17592186364551 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364552 13194139535745 true] [17592186364551 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364553 13194139535745 true] [17592186364551 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364554 13194139535745 true] [17592186364551 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364555 13194139535745 true] [17592186364551 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364556 13194139535745 true] [17592186364551 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535745 true] [17592186364551 1041 "se